perf based replacement for autofdo to generate profile feedback data for gcc's -fauto-profile option.

Eventual goal is to support an online modus that supports contiguous profiling of the system
and then rebuilding pieces with profile feedback.

Requires a gcc patched with https://github.com/andikleen/gcc libbacktrace-disc-* patches

Build libbacktrace with above branch if needed:
git checkout -b libbacktrace-disc-6 https://github.com/andikleen/gcc gcc-lb  # or latest branch
mkdir obj
cd obj
../gcc-lb/configure --enable-languages=c,c++
cd libbacktrace
make -j $(nproc)

To build perf-gcov:
git checkout https://github.com/andikleen/perf-gcov
cd perf-gcov
copy gcc-objdir/libbacktrace/.libs/libbacktrace.a to gcov build directory
make

Synopsis:

gcc -g -O2 -o workload ...
perf record -b -c 100003 -e branches:upp workload
gcov.py --binary workload --gcov file.gcov
gcc -fauto-profile=file.gcov -o workload.opt -O2 -g ...

Testing:

(if autofdo is installed will print reference output, otherwise runs on its own)

./tester

Status:

Needs fixes

Update to new proposed gcc gcov format?
